  "id": "forensic-neuropsychology",
  "term": "forensic neuropsychology",
  "definition": "Forensic neuropsychology is the use of neuropsychological knowledge and testing in forensic practice. In this context, it focuses on assessing cognitive and related brain-behavior functions in offenders, such as executive functioning, attention, language, social processes, and reward or threat processing.",
